// Package cybericebox.brain.v1 is the Brain service contract: the gRPC protocol a client (the platform
// backend today, any client tomorrow) uses to drive the closed Brain project. Brain is the SERVER; the
// client calls in. Method names read as the ACTION the CLIENT performs. This is the MACHINE control
// plane only.
//
// HOME: the generated Go is committed in the PUBLIC platform backend repo as package
// github.com/cybericebox/backend/pkg/brainapi/v1 (the backend repo is public and its CI cannot fetch a
// private module). The private Brain imports the SAME package, so it gets no backend internals — only
// this generated contract compiles into it. The .proto is AUTHORED by the Brain side and landed into
// that package by the backend; both generate from one source of truth.
//
// TWO TRANSPORTS, by fit:
//   - gRPC (this file): the typed machine control plane — enrollment, runs (grader + opponents),
//     capability ("give me an opponent"), statistics ingest, the outbox (one bidi stream) and the
//     task-archive upload.
//   - A SEPARATE HTTP/SSE chat handle (NOT here): the authoring CONVERSATION and its session lifecycle
//     (open/message/start/stop/save/attachments/events/archive) are browser-driven through the client's
//     /v1/assistant proxy. The client proxies it; it is intentionally absent from this proto.
//
// TWO ENDPOINTS: the gRPC control endpoint and the HTTP/SSE chat endpoint are separate ports in the
// stored connection (grpc_endpoint + the http endpoint) — no single-port ALPN mux.
//
// The brain<->pad (runner) link is a DIFFERENT gRPC service (internal to Brain + the lab).
//
// SUBJECT: the gRPC control calls are TENANT-scoped (mTLS CN = tenant), never user-scoped — no
// "x-subject" metadata. User authority travels IN-MESSAGE on the outbox provide_* requests, which the
// brain ORIGINATES (provide_lab.subject / provide_task.subject / provide_device.subject); the client authorizes against that. The
// chat's per-user subject (X-Cib-Subject) rides the SEPARATE HTTP/SSE transport, not here.
//
// ERROR MODEL (RPC status): InvalidArgument (bad/oversized/unsupported-media input); Unauthenticated
// (missing/invalid client cert); PermissionDenied; NotFound (unknown run/session/task; reason="gone"
// for a hard-deleted/expired one); AlreadyExists = idempotent SUCCESS (a repeat of StartRun,
// UploadMaterials, PostLabFacts, a verdict, an answer, an archive upload); FailedPrecondition (e.g. a
// session/archive not ready); ResourceExhausted (+ RetryInfo) for rate limits; Unavailable for
// transient. Clients retry ONLY Unavailable/ResourceExhausted/network. A stable machine reason rides in
// google.rpc.ErrorInfo. Deadlines: unary 30 s; best-effort StopRun/PostLabFacts 5 s; streams have no
// deadline and are never closed by age. Keepalive: client ping 30 s; server MinTime <= 20 s; no
// server-level heartbeats. Message sizes: unary up to 16 MiB (PushData batches split by size); stream
